{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"storeURI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Device-local by design: it must never be synced, exported, or adopted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from another device’s data. Object URIs carry a store UUID and primary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key, so a foreign URI is meaningless here at best — and on a device","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restored from another device’s backup (matching store UUID) it can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resolve to the wrong object. Entries are disposable: a missing or stale","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"URI is re-populated wherever the object surfaces next — attach import,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"save capture, or integration creating the object for an insert change.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(An update or delete change whose identifier has no usable URI is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skipped for that pass, not re-resolved.)"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/globalidentifier\/storeuri"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The local object’s "},{"code":"NSManagedObjectID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" URI — the essential mapping from","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"this global identifier to its row in THIS device’s persistent store,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used by integration to locate the object for incoming changes."}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GlobalIdentifier"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GlobalIdentifier\/storeURI"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"storeURI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"storeURI","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:9Ensembles16GlobalIdentifierV8storeURISSSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/GlobalIdentifier":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A globally unique identifier for a synced object.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GlobalIdentifier","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/globalidentifier","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlobalIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"GlobalIdentifier","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlobalIdentifier"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles","type":"topic","title":"Ensembles","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sync Core Data and SwiftData stores across devices using event sourcing."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/GlobalIdentifier/storeURI":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GlobalIdentifier\/storeURI","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The local object’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObjectID"},{"type":"text","te